WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.398
Parallel Structure and Logical Comparisons

00:00:03.778 --> 00:00:07.194
Lists match. Comparisons compare like with like.

00:00:08.394 --> 00:00:09.392
How to spot it

00:00:09.792 --> 00:00:12.010
A list or pair with one item missing

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:14.161
Or a comparison with “than”

00:00:14.711 --> 00:00:18.732
It’s testing: matching forms and logical comparisons

00:00:19.932 --> 00:00:20.727
The method

00:00:21.127 --> 00:00:23.616
Step 1: Find the other items

00:00:23.896 --> 00:00:24.937
What form are they?

00:00:25.487 --> 00:00:27.521
Step 2: Copy the form

00:00:27.801 --> 00:00:30.861
-ing, “to” + verb, noun or past tense.

00:00:31.411 --> 00:00:34.762
Step 3: Name both sides of a comparison

00:00:35.042 --> 00:00:38.342
Diet vs diet, not diet vs people.

00:00:38.892 --> 00:00:41.572
Step 4: Fix with that of / those of

00:00:41.852 --> 00:00:44.928
One thing: that. Many: those.

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:46.587
In a few words

00:00:46.737 --> 00:00:48.951
Match the form. Match the thing.

00:00:50.151 --> 00:00:50.974
The rules

00:00:51.374 --> 00:00:52.712
Lists use one form

00:00:52.992 --> 00:00:56.059
Wrong: to ask, examining, and draw

00:00:56.339 --> 00:00:59.630
Right: to ask, to examine, and to draw

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:01.049
Pairs match

00:01:01.329 --> 00:01:05.201
Right: not only to cut costs but also to improve care

00:01:05.751 --> 00:01:07.039
Compare like with like

00:01:07.319 --> 00:01:11.003
Wrong: Tokyo’s population is larger than New York.

00:01:11.283 --> 00:01:13.588
Right: larger than that of New York

00:01:14.138 --> 00:01:16.732
that of = one, those of = many

00:01:17.012 --> 00:01:20.412
Right: her songs are longer than those of other singers

00:01:21.612 --> 00:01:22.653
Let’s try one

00:01:23.081 --> 00:01:29.510
Studies of ancient DNA show that the diet of early farmers in the region was less varied than ______

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:33.663
What’s being compared? The diet of early farmers.

00:01:34.213 --> 00:01:40.226
Diet versus people: A. Those is plural: C. And D isn’t grammatical.

00:01:40.776 --> 00:01:45.587
That of the hunter-gatherers: a diet compared to a diet. Choice B.

00:01:46.787 --> 00:01:47.782
Common traps

00:01:48.182 --> 00:01:49.470
Thing vs person

00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:53.531
“Her paintings are brighter than Monet.” Compare paintings.

00:01:54.081 --> 00:01:55.089
The mixed list

00:01:55.369 --> 00:01:57.032
One item in a different form.

00:01:58.232 --> 00:02:01.031
Parallel Structure and Logical Comparisons

00:02:01.311 --> 00:02:03.525
Match the form. Match the thing.

00:02:04.075 --> 00:02:04.847
Spot it

00:02:05.047 --> 00:02:08.655
List or pair missing an item, or a “than” comparison

00:02:09.205 --> 00:02:09.912
Steps

00:02:10.112 --> 00:02:12.678
1. Find the form of the other items

00:02:12.958 --> 00:02:15.192
2. Copy that form exactly

00:02:15.472 --> 00:02:18.114
3. Name both sides of a comparison

00:02:18.394 --> 00:02:20.636
4. Fix with that of / those of

00:02:21.186 --> 00:02:21.939
Remember

00:02:22.139 --> 00:02:25.932
Lists: one form (to ask, to examine, to draw)

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:28.749
not only … but also … must match

00:02:29.029 --> 00:02:30.317
Compare like with like

00:02:30.597 --> 00:02:33.336
that of = one; those of = many

00:02:33.886 --> 00:02:34.491
Trap

00:02:34.691 --> 00:02:36.369
Comparing a thing to a person

00:02:37.119 --> 00:02:40.814
